From 7358594d5a6fc9c69f1730357ec26706bdb3ed5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "lpm maintainer (Claude)" <maintainer@lpm.local>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 02:20:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lpkg: fix bsdtar invocation packing data.tar.zst
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: lpkg_pack_one() built the bsdtar command line as

    bsdtar -C <pkgdir> -czf <out> --zstd .

which passes two conflicting compression-filter selectors: -z
(bundled into -czf) requests gzip, --zstd requests zstd. bsdtar
rejects any combination of a short compression flag with a long
compression-filter option, since both attempt to choose the filter,
and refuses with 'Can't specify both -z and --zstd'. This made
'lpm package build'/'lpm package pack' fail 100% of the time on any
system with bsdtar installed, right after 'packing files...'.

Fix: drop -z and keep -c (create) + -f (file) plus --zstd, which
already selects the correct filter on its own and matches the
data.tar.zst output name:

    bsdtar -C <pkgdir> --zstd -cf <out> .

No other command in the tree combines a short compression flag with
a long filter option (checked every bsdtar/tar invocation in src/).
The extraction side already reads data.tar.zst via bsdtar's format
auto-detection (bsdtar -xf, no -z/--zstd needed there), so it already
expected genuinely zstd-compressed input and needs no change. The
tar+zstd fallback path used when bsdtar isn't installed was never
affected.

Verified against the actual reported transcript: built the pre-fix
binary and reproduced the exact 'bsdtar: Can'\''t specify both -z and
--zstd' / 'failed to pack data' failure through a bsdtar shim that
enforces the same flag-conflict rule; rebuilt with the fix and
confirmed 'lpm package pack' and 'lpm package build' both complete,
produce a correctly structured .lpkg (meta + sha256 + data.tar.zst),
and sign successfully.

Files changed:
- src/lpkg.c        — the one-line command fix
- CHANGELOG.md       — Unreleased/Fixed entry (behavior changed: pack
                       now succeeds instead of always failing)
---
 CHANGELOG.md |  13 +++++++++++++
 lpm          | Bin 213448 -> 213448 bytes
 src/lpkg.c   |   2 +-
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index f459696..a20a182 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **lpkg.c** — `lpm package build`/`lpm package pack` failed on every
+  system with `bsdtar` installed: `error: failed to pack data for
+  <pkg>` (`bsdtar: Can't specify both -z and --zstd`). The
+  `data.tar.zst` packing step passed both `-z` (gzip) and `--zstd`
+  to `bsdtar`, two mutually exclusive compression-filter selectors.
+  Dropped `-z` — `--zstd` alone already selects the correct filter,
+  matching the `.tar.zst` output name. The `tar`+`zstd` fallback path
+  (used when `bsdtar` isn't installed) was unaffected.
+
